[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged as one issue because the reports share subject lines
([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)). Read by where each report comes from
(its tenant's locale and booking form), it holds three problems with three different fixes.
Each has a ticket of its own.

<Callout kind="warn">
Engineering closed #4471 on 5 October: <code>parser</code> fixed (fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu
locales), <code>hint</code> won't fix (booking-v3 form retired). Neither covers the
<code>one-day</code> reports. That ticket stays open.
</Callout>

## The split

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {issues} />

## How it is counted

- Report ids are unique: the export pages overlap, so repeated rows count once.
- A report is placed by its **tenant**, not by the intake tag (a guess from the reporter's browser).
- `hint`: a form booking at a tenant whose booking form prints a month-first hint.
- `one-day`: reports the desk read as a one-day move (`desk-notes.json`). Their dates move by
  one day in the same month, which no day/month order explains.
- Every number on this page is computed from the data at render time.

## The desk's view

The desk counts by tenant alone, so the `one-day` reports sit under `parser` there, with a
footnote. The tickets carry these counts.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## What changes for the desk

- A closed #4471 does not mean every wrong-date report is answered: send one-day moves to the
  `one-day` ticket.
- A new report about a wrong date goes to the problem its tenant and channel point to, not to the
  ticket with the same subject.

<RenderStamp {signature} />
